Test-only capability services for tests/sys/mac_capability:

  keystore/     mac_capability_test_keystore    async key-value store
  kernelstore/  mac_capability_test_kernelstore sync shared key-value store
  cleanup/      mac_capability_test_cleanup     unload/cleanup ordering probe
  include/      wire protocols shared with the test programs

They are built by buildkernel from sys/modules/mac_capability_test_* when
tests are enabled (MK_TESTS, or ALL_MODULES), with Makefile.fixture here:
they install in /usr/tests/sys/mac_capability/fixtures, off the kernel
module path, and are packaged in mac-capability-tests, never in a kernel
package.  Production code does not include their headers.

The cases load them by absolute path; no loader configuration is needed.
A keystore or kernelstore case loads its fixture the first time it connects
(require_fixture() in mac_capability_test_helpers.h), and the fixture stays
loaded; the unload and cleanup cases load and unload
mac_capability_test_cleanup themselves.  A missing or refused fixture fails
the case.  The fixtures register test services: run the suite only in a
disposable test guest, never on a host whose capability plane is in
production use.
